cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using these metadata and cite the associated article when it is available."
title: "False-alarm calibration transport across engines in full-flight aero-engine anomaly detection (N-CMAPSS): code, frozen protocols and evidence"
version: 1.1.0
# doi: to be added after the v1.1.0 release is archived (Zenodo); see docs/release/v1.1.0/RELEASE_NOTES.md
authors:
  - family-names: Mei
    given-names: Jinghang
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2901-3285
    affiliation: "School of Electrical and Computer Engineering, The University of Sydney"
repository-code: https://github.com/surnamemei/ncmapss-phase-entanglement
license: MIT
keywords:
  - condition monitoring
  - false-alarm calibration
  - calibration transport
  - anomaly detection
  - aero-engine
  - N-CMAPSS
  - nonstationary operating conditions
abstract: >-
  Research code, frozen protocols, calibration-only locks, one-shot audit records, derived outputs and an evidence
  ledger for an audit of nominal healthy false-alarm calibration in full-flight aero-engine anomaly detection on
  N-CMAPSS: DS02 discovery, a frozen one-shot DS03 confirmation, separately frozen post-confirmation analyses, a frozen
  multi-subset extension over seven previously unopened subsets (five fleet families, 30 held-out audit engines), an
  internal hostile review and a final author-approved focused validation. Raw NASA data are not redistributed.
